    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4164" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλίγκιος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>resembling, like</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀστέρι καλῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.401
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἀθανάτοισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.174
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴδεα πᾶσιν ἀ.</span>, of
			paintings, <i><span class="en">
				Emp.
				23.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σοὶ φυὰν ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					B.
					5.168
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀνειράτων ἀ. μορφαῖσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					449
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἡρώεσσιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1356
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arat.
				462
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.966
			</span></i>, etc.:—but compd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐναλίγκιος</span> is more freq.</div>
